    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0564" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20252/12–644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-06T18:00:00+01:00">December 6, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 7—1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3961. Despatch 3389, November 9.<anchor n="83" xml:id="d601-f1"/> A note has now
                    been received from the Spanish Foreign Office dated November 27 in reply to
                    Embassy’s <hi rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> 827, November 6 supplying
                    lists of names of the following: <list>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                        <item>53 German agents expelled from North Africa plus 5 who are to leave
                            shortly. This list includes name of an unknown individual not appearing
                            in Tangier’s despatch 2470, November 25;<anchor n="83" xml:id="d601-f2"
                            />
                        </item>
                        <pb facs="0565" n="553" xml:id="pg553"/>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                        <item>36 German agents ordered interned at Caldas and 3 ordered interned at
                            other unspecified places about which we propose to get specific
                            data;</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)</label>
                        <item>750 German customs guards and officials transferred to Sobrón from
                            Miranda concentration camp, the remaining 500 others at Miranda, names
                            of whom are promised. Reourtel 3807, November 21, 3 p.m. Despatch
                                follows.<anchor n="84" xml:id="d601-f3"/>
                        </item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Following oral representations to the Under Secretary the Foreign Office includes
                    written undertaking that orders have been given prohibiting interned foreigners
                    from using the interurban telephone.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tangier by courier.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
